Root cause: Micromodal's click listener treats any click on an element with data-micromodal-close (including the overlay) as a request to close the modal, without checking if the click originated from inside the modal content. When a checkbox is activated via Space, a click event bubbles up to the overlay, causing the modal to close prematurely and preventing the checkbox toggle.

Repair strategy: Modify the onClick handler to ignore overlay clicks when the event target is not the overlay itself (i.e., the click came from inside the modal). Close button clicks remain unaffected because their target is the close button, not the overlay.

Expected accessibility effect: Pressing Space on a checkbox inside the modal will now toggle the checkbox without closing the modal, preserving keyboard operability and maintaining visible focus within the dialog, satisfying WCAG 2.1.1 (Keyboard) and 2.4.3 (Focus Order).

Functional risks: Changing click handling could affect legitimate overlay clicks (e.g., clicking on the backdrop) – we preserve those. There is a risk if the modal structure changes and the overlay lacks the 'modal__overlay' class, but that's internal to the component. Also, programmatic clicks on the overlay from scripts would still close as intended.

